<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml" xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:CafePos.Presentation.ViewModels;assembly=CafePos.Presentation" x:Class="CafePosApp.Views.ShiftReportPage"
             x:Name="ShiftReportPageRoot" x:DataType="vm:ShiftReportViewModel" Title="Смена"
             Shell.NavBarIsVisible="False">
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         THE WHOLE PAGE SCROLLS. The owner's decision, and it is settled — read this before
         "fixing" the missing ScrollView.

         This page HAD one and it was deliberately REMOVED, to hand the leftover height to a
         recycling CollectionView: the list was the only `*` row, so it received whatever the Auto
         rows above it left behind. That is arithmetic, and it is how this page broke. Content
         above the list grew until «История заказов смены» had no height left at all — the list
         rendered no rows and there was nothing to scroll — and what it did have was a cramped
         window scrolling inside itself. Recycling was never the bug. The layout that served it was.

         So there is ONE scroller again, and the list renders its FULL content inside it. A
         CollectionView inside a ScrollView must be handed an explicit HeightRequest guessed from an
         item count, which is either wrong today or a maintenance trap the next time a row changes
         height, so the list is a BindableLayout on a VerticalStackLayout instead — the idiom
         already used for the item lines inside each card below, and on SettingsPage and the
         catalogue forms. The list measures itself, so NO part of this layout depends on how much
         height is left over: a short phone, landscape and a tall one all behave the same.

         The trade-off, stated here rather than discovered later: nothing on this list recycles. It
         is bounded — one shift's closed orders — so rendering it whole is affordable, and the
         alternative costs a guessed pixel count on every future edit to the list.

         Do not remove this ScrollView a third time without knowing the verdict above.
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <ScrollView>
        <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto" Padding="16" RowSpacing="10">
            <!-- No toolbar row. «Обновить» is gone by the owner's decision, and it was the only
             thing this row held — it duplicated leaving and re-entering the page. Nothing is
             lost by removing it: this page has no polling, and OnAppearing reloads, so
             navigating away and back is a complete manual reload. The Shell nav bar is hidden
             here too (Shell.NavBarIsVisible on this page): it repeated the "Смена" tab label,
             and the tab bar is what names the section. Which is also why the page now carries a
             heading of its own — hiding the nav bar took the last line that said where the
             operator was, and nothing replaced it. -->
            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                 WHICH SHIFT THIS IS, AND SINCE WHEN.

                 The page used to open straight onto the summary card, so the figures at the top
                 belonged to a shift nobody could identify: a report read at the end of one shift
                 and one read at the start of the next were the same screen. A drawer total is
                 only meaningful against the shift it was counted for.

                 «Смена открыта 03.10.2026 11:22» is ShiftReportViewModel.StartTimeText — a
                 property that ALREADY existed and was bound NOWHERE on the page, even though
                 LoadAsync raises it on both paths. So this heading needed no ViewModel change at
                 all: the property was already there, formatted, already doing the ToLocalTime()
                 that Shift.StartTime requires of it (it is UTC, migration 3 — the same trap
                 OrderRowViewModel.CreatedAtText documents for order times).

                 The period has a start and no end, and that is not an omission: this page's route
                 carries no shift id and it rebinds to whatever shift is open, so it can only ever
                 show the OPEN one. The «Завершённая · 03.10.2026 11:22 – 11:43» half of the
                 analytics page's shift label belongs to a page that can read a closed shift.
                 With no shift open the text is empty and only the heading shows, which is the
                 honest thing to say: there is no period to report. -->
            <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="0" Spacing="0">
                <Label Text="Отчёт по смене" Style="{StaticResource PageTitle}" />
                <Label Text="{Binding StartTimeText}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                       LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
            </VerticalStackLayout>
            <!-- Static value, so an AppThemeBinding on the attribute is the whole fix and needs no ViewModel
                 change. A bare {StaticResource Danger} declared the light token in both themes: this
                 label sits on the page fill (#FAFAFA / #121212), where that is 4.77:1 in light and
                 3.76:1 in dark against the 4.5:1 owed at 14pt. DangerDark #FF9E8E on #121212 is
                 9.40:1. -->
            <Label Grid.Row="1" Text="{Binding Message}" IsVisible="{Binding HasMessage}"
                   TextColor="{AppThemeBinding Light={StaticResource Danger}, Dark={StaticResource DangerDark}}"
                   LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
                <Border Grid.Row="2" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}">
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6">
                        <Label Text="{Binding RevenueText, StringFormat='Выручка: {0}'}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding ClosedOrdersCount, StringFormat='Чеков: {0}'}" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding CancelledOrdersCount, StringFormat='Отменено: {0}'}" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding AverageCheckText, StringFormat='Средний чек: {0}'}" />
    
                        <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                             MONEY THROUGH THE TILL.
    
                             These four Payments* figures on ShiftStats existed since the payments
                             feature and were consumed ONLY by the CSV export — «Принято оплат» had
                             never been on screen at all. That is fine until there are refunds: revenue
                             falls, the export grows a «Возвращено» line, and without this the operator
                             watches the money leave with nothing on the device to reconcile the drawer
                             against. This block is the on-screen twin of the export's, and it must keep
                             the export's GROSS wording: "Принято" always means what came in, never what
                             is left.
    
                             All inside the existing summary card, which the brief's "Auto" row absorbs
                             without a grid change. A divider rather than a nested card: a Border
                             inside a Border reads as two competing surfaces on one block, and the
                             grouping only has to be legible, not boxed.
                             ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
                        <BoxView HeightRequest="1" Margin="0,4,0,2" Color="{AppThemeBinding Light={StaticResource Gray300}, Dark={StaticResource Gray700}}" />
                        <Label Text="Деньги" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,2" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding PaymentsCashText, StringFormat='Принято наличными: {0}'}" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding PaymentsCardText, StringFormat='Принято картой: {0}'}" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding RefundsCashText, StringFormat='Возвращено наличными: {0}'}" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding RefundsCardText, StringFormat='Возвращено картой: {0}'}" />

                        <!-- The two movements that are not orders. Placed WITH the components of the
                             total rather than in a section of their own, because the operator's job
                             here is to check the sum by eye: change in, minus cash carried out, plus
                             what came through the till, and that has to be readable as one block.

                             Both are NET of corrections, so an uncorrected mistake and a corrected one
                             show the same figure here — and differ only in the list below, which is
                             the point: the totals are for reconciling, the list is for investigating. -->
                        <Label Text="{Binding FloatCashText, StringFormat='Внесено размена: {0}'}" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding PayoutCashText, StringFormat='Изъято на инкассацию: {0}'}" />

                        <!-- The drawer total. TWO lines, and that is the fix rather than a layout
                             preference: it used to be one label, «Итого наличными в кассе: {0}» at
                             20pt bold, and the caption plus the amount do not both fit across a
                             360dp card — the number the page exists for wrapped onto a second
                             line under its own words, which is the worst possible break on the
                             one figure the operator came to read. On a line of its own the amount
                             has the whole width of the card to itself and simply fits; the
                             caption, which may wrap harmlessly, gets a whole line too, and its
                             wrapping no longer moves the number anywhere.

                             The caption is a SectionTitle so the total reads as the card's
                             conclusion and not as one more component of it: the components above
                             are 14pt body text under «Деньги», this is what they add up to.

                             Not coloured: the emphasis is size and weight, and the caption above
                             already says what the number is, so nothing here depends on colour to
                             be read. The description rides on the VALUE and not on the card —
                             a container with a contentDescription is announced as a single node
                             and its children stop being traversed (see ShiftAnalyticsPage), which
                             would have cost the caption as well. -->
                        <Label Text="Итого наличными в кассе" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
                        <Label Text="{Binding CashInDrawerText}"
                               FontSize="20" FontAttributes="Bold"
                               SemanticProperties.Description="Итого наличными в кассе: внесён размен плюс принято наличными, минус возвращено наличными и изъято на инкассацию" />
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </Border>

                <!-- THE DRAWER ACTIONS. Two buttons and no more: put change in, take cash out. Both
                     are reachable only with a shift open, and the layout says so by disappearing
                     rather than by showing two disabled buttons an operator has to read past.
                     Correction is not here either — it is per-row, on the movement being corrected,
                     because "cancel a movement" is meaningless without naming which one.

                     A STACK, not two columns, and the 360dp measurement is why. As
                     ColumnDefinitions="*,*" each button got about 160dp for its label, and
                     «Изъять на инкассацию» needs more than that: the device showed «Изъять на» with
                     the second word cut off by the button's own edge, on the one control here that
                     moves money OUT of the till. Full width gives both labels the whole content
                     column instead of half of it, and unlike a re-proportioned Grid ("Auto,*" sized
                     to its text, "1.3*,*") it does not depend on how the text happens to measure —
                     a caption that grows with the platform's font scale, a narrower phone or a
                     longer translation cannot push it back under the edge.

                     THE DANGEROUS ONE LOOKS DANGEROUS. It was the same violet Primary as
                     «Внести размен» and «Анализировать смену», so carrying cash out of the till
                     was indistinguishable from putting cash in or from reading a report. It takes
                     the app's existing DangerButton — the same style «Закрыть смену» wears at the
                     bottom of this page and the same one the per-movement «Отменить движение» wears
                     on each row below — so no new colour enters the palette. Money coming IN is
                     SecondaryButton, the grey tonal every other non-primary action wears, and in
                     dark theme the two now differ the way they do in light: by the plate. The dark
                     DangerButton is a pale DangerDark fill with black lettering against the neutral
                     Gray800 of SecondaryButton, which is the app's one dark-theme rule for an
                     emphasised action (PrimaryDark + Black on the primary buttons) — see the
                     measurements on DangerButton in Styles.xaml. It used to be Gray800 + DangerDark
                     against Gray800 + Gray100: the same grey plate twice, told apart by a tint of the
                     letters. «Анализировать смену» stays Primary — it is the page's one navigation
                     action and touches no money at all — so the three read as navigate / safe /
                     destructive in both themes now. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="3" Spacing="8" IsVisible="{Binding HasOpenShift}">
                    <Button Text="Внести размен" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryButton}"
                            Command="{Binding AddFloatCommand}"
                            SemanticProperties.Description="Положить наличные в кассу как размен" />
                    <Button Text="Изъять на инкассацию" Style="{StaticResource DangerButton}"
                            Command="{Binding AddPayoutCommand}"
                            SemanticProperties.Description="Забрать наличные из кассы на инкассацию. На эту сумму уменьшится остаток в кассе." />
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- The movement list. Present because a drawer figure with nothing behind it cannot
                     be investigated: a shortage is one number, and this is what says whether it is a
                     missed collection, a mistyped amount or change nobody counted in. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="4" Spacing="4" IsVisible="{Binding HasOpenShift}">
                    <Label Text="Движения по кассе" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
                    <!-- LEFT-ALIGNED HERE, NOT IN EmptyLabel. The global style centres every empty
                         state in the app, and this page's text is left-aligned everywhere else, so a
                         centred sentence under a heading read as a different design language rather
                         than as an empty state. The override is LOCAL on purpose: whether the other
                         empty states want centring is a decision about the app, not a fix to smuggle
                         in from here, so the shared style is untouched. -->
                    <Label Text="Движений по кассе не было." Style="{StaticResource EmptyLabel}"
                           HorizontalTextAlignment="Start"
                           IsVisible="{Binding HasNoCashMovements}" />
                    <!-- ROWS ARE CARDS, like the order history below. This list used to be bare text
                         on the page fill: no border, no fill, Spacing="0". «Размен / +5580.00 ₿ /
                         11:22» floated under the heading with nothing around it, one row looked like
                         a paragraph that had been cut off before it started, and two lists drawn two
                         different ways on one screen read as two different apps.
                         CardBorder is the very style the history cards use below — same fill, stroke,
                         radius and padding — and the 4dp bottom Margin is the gap those cards
                         already use, which is why this stack keeps Spacing="0". A full outline on
                         every row also reads correctly at ONE row, where a divider between rows
                         would have had nothing to divide. -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding CashMovements}" Spacing="0">
                        <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:CashMovementRow">
                                <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                                     THE ROW TAP IS GONE.

                                     Every row used to carry a TapGestureRecognizer bound to
                                     CancelMovementCommand, so a touch anywhere on the row — on the
                                     title, on the amount, on the empty part of the card — asked
                                     «Отменить движение?». Nothing on the row said that was there:
                                     no icon, no label, no pressed state. And the act is not an edit:
                                     the row stays where it is and a reversing entry appears beside
                                     it, which is harder to undo than the mistake was to make. Making
                                     the row a card (§4.1) made it worse — a card is drawn as
                                     something an operator picks up, and picking this one up
                                     rewrites the ledger.

                                     An unnamed gesture on a whole row is a bad way to expose an
                                     irreversible action whatever it is called, so the tap was not
                                     given a sign and kept: the action is a control with its own name
                                     on it now, at the bottom of the card. The confirmation dialog is
                                     untouched — this row is presentation only, and so is the row
                                     structure: the wrapper VerticalStackLayout that used to sit
                                     around the Border existed only to host <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                                     and is gone with it, which leaves a Border at the root of the
                                     template, exactly like the order history cards below.
                                     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
                                <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                                    <!-- NESTED LAYOUTS, not one Grid with ColumnSpan. ColumnSpan is a
                                         Layout property: putting it on a Label is a XamlParseException at
                                         the moment the first row is realised, which surfaced as «Не удалось
                                         загрузить смену» with every figure above it already updated.
                                         The reason needs the full width and the header needs two columns,
                                         and a stack of two Grids says that without asking one element to
                                         have a property it does not have. -->
                                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="2">
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                            <Label Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding Title}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                            <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding AmountText}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                        </Grid>
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                            <Label Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding TimeText}" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                                   VerticalTextAlignment="Center" />
                                            <!-- «отмена» as a pill, so the two kinds of row are told
                                                 apart by shape and not only by a grey word in the
                                                 corner. The plain Tag style, NOT TagWarning: a
                                                 reversed movement is a FACT about the ledger, and
                                                 an orange pill would claim it is a warning — the
                                                 word carries the state, the pill only marks it.
                                                 Same column and same right edge as the amount
                                                 above, so a pill appearing cannot shift the
                                                 amount out from under the eye. -->
                                            <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource Tag}"
                                                    VerticalOptions="Center"
                                                    IsVisible="{Binding IsCorrection}">
                                                <Label Text="отмена" Style="{StaticResource TagText}" />
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                        <!-- Wraps through as many lines as it needs: on a 360dp
                                             card a long reason ran to four, which is exactly why
                                             it sits on its own line under the header instead of
                                             inside the two-column grid. -->
                                        <Label Text="{Binding ReasonText}" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                               LineBreakMode="WordWrap"
                                               IsVisible="{Binding ReasonText, Converter={StaticResource IsPresent}}" />

                                        <!-- THE CONTROL THE TAP USED TO HIDE BEHIND.
                                             FULL WIDTH, because there is nothing to put beside it and a
                                             half-width button with an empty cell next to it reads as a
                                             layout accident. «Отменить движение» rather than a bare
                                             «Отменить»: this page carries three destructive controls —
                                             this one, «Отмена» on an order, «Закрыть смену» — and the
                                             label has to say which one is being pressed BEFORE the press.
                                             DangerButton, the same style «Закрыть смену» wears at the
                                             bottom of the page, so reversing a ledger entry and
                                             closing a shift are visibly the same class of act.
                                             48dp, not the 44 this style inherits: the whole point of
                                             moving the action out of the row is that it is meant to be
                                             pressed deliberately.

                                             HIDDEN ON A CORRECTION. CancelMovementAsync refuses those
                                             outright («Отменить отмену нельзя»), and a control whose
                                             only possible outcome is a refusal is the thing the order
                                             void spent its previous life getting rid of — the same
                                             reasoning CanCancel carries on the history cards below.
                                             The «отмена» pill already says the row is a correction,
                                             so nothing is lost by not offering the action.

                                             THE DESCRIPTION NAMES THE ROW AND THE CONSEQUENCE, because a
                                             button announces itself and nothing else to a screen
                                             reader. DescribeForConfirmation is the very string the
                                             confirmation dialog opens with, so what is heard and
                                             what is then read cannot disagree.

                                             The command comes through the page's own x:Name, never
                                             RelativeSource AncestorType={vm:ShiftReportViewModel}:
                                             that form makes the XAML runtime construct the type, and
                                             this ViewModel comes from DI. -->
                                        <Button Text="Отменить движение" Style="{StaticResource DangerButton}"
                                                Margin="0,6,0,0" MinimumHeightRequest="48"
                                                Command="{Binding Source={x:Reference ShiftReportPageRoot}, Path=BindingContext.CancelMovementCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding .}"
                                                IsVisible="{Binding IsCorrection, Converter={StaticResource InvertedBoolConverter}}"
                                                SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding DescribeForConfirmation, StringFormat='Отменить движение: {0}. Запись не изменится — рядом появится корректирующая.'}" />
                                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                                </Border>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- No shift: the report has nothing to describe, and an empty report of an empty shift
                     is indistinguishable from a report of a quiet one. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="3" Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding HasOpenShift, Converter={StaticResource InvertedBoolConverter}}">
                    <Button Text="Открыть смену" Command="{Binding OpenShiftCommand}" />
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <Button Grid.Row="5" Text="Анализировать смену" Command="{Binding OpenAnalyticsCommand}" />
                <Label Grid.Row="6" Text="История заказов смены" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
                <!-- ShiftHistory, not CompletedOrders: it is GetShiftOrderHistoryAsync's Completed AND
                     Cancelled, so a voided sale shows up AS voided instead of disappearing from the
                     only list a manager reads after the fact.

                     BindableLayout, not a CollectionView: the trade-off of putting the list
                     inside the page ScrollView is spelled out at the top of this file. One
                     scroller, one gesture, and the list is as tall as the orders it holds.
                     Spacing 0 because the 4dp between cards is already on each Border.
                     SelectionMode="None" went with it — a BindableLayout has no selection
                     to disable, and it was already the default for these rows. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="7" BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding ShiftHistory}" Spacing="0">
                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:OrderRowViewModel">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="4">
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
                                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="1">
                                            <Label Text="{Binding OrderTitle}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                            <!-- The status is on the card because the list now contains
                                                 voided orders. Without it a cancelled sale and a
                                                 completed one were visually identical — same rows, same
                                                 total, same date — and the one the manager needs to
                                                 identify is the one that says nothing about itself.
                                                 CancellationReason rides along, because the domain
                                                 composes the money and the stock disposition into it. -->
                                            <Label Text="{Binding StatusText}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                   TextColor="{Binding StatusColor}" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                                   SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding StatusHint}" />
                                            <!-- The composed cancellation reason: how much came back and
                                                 what happened to the stock. "Отменен" alone tells a
                                                 manager the order is gone and nothing about where the
                                                 money went. -->
                                            <Label Text="{Binding CancellationDetail}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                   IsVisible="{Binding CancellationDetail, Converter={StaticResource IsPresent}}"
                                                   LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
                                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                                        <!-- CreatedAtText, not StringFormat on Model.CreatedAt. The
                                             raw DateTimeOffset is UTC (migration 3), and StringFormat
                                             renders it without a zone conversion — so the same order
                                             read 18:46 on the orders board and 16:46 in this history
                                             on a UTC+2 device. The binding was valid, so no build
                                             caught it; OrderRowViewModel.CreatedAtText already does
                                             the ToLocalTime() the orders page relies on. -->
                                        <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding CreatedAtText}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" />
                                    </Grid>
                                    <VerticalStackLayout BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding ItemLines}" Spacing="3">
                                        <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:OrderItemLine">
                                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8" Padding="0,0,2,0">
                                                    <Label Text="{Binding Name}" LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
                                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Quantity, StringFormat='× {0}'}" FontAttributes="Bold" VerticalTextAlignment="Start" />
                                                </Grid>
                                            </DataTemplate>
                                        </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                                    <Label Text="{Binding TotalPriceText, StringFormat='Итого: {0}'}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                        <!-- "Подробнее" exists because the void flow and the payment
                                             ledger both live on the details page, and a history row that
                                             showed a total with no way to see how it was paid left the
                                             manager to trust the card. -->
                                        <Button Text="Подробнее" Padding="8,6" MinimumHeightRequest="48"
                                                Command="{Binding Source={RelativeSource AncestorType={x:Type ContentPage}}, Path=BindingContext.OpenDetailsCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding .}"
                                                SemanticProperties.Description="Открыть детали заказа" />
                                        <!-- The void action. Only on rows that are not already cancelled
                                             (CanCancel), so an order that was already voided cannot be
                                             voided again — the domain would refuse it, but the control
                                             that can only fail is the thing this feature spent its
                                             previous life removing. DangerButton for the same reason the
                                             board's cancel is: cancelling destroys a sale. -->
                                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding CancelText}" Style="{StaticResource DangerButton}"
                                                Padding="8,6" MinimumHeightRequest="48"
                                                Command="{Binding Source={RelativeSource AncestorType={x:Type ContentPage}}, Path=BindingContext.CancelOrderCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding .}" IsVisible="{Binding CanCancel}"
                                                SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding CancelHint}" />
                                    </Grid>
                                </VerticalStackLayout>
                            </Border>
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- The empty state CollectionView.EmptyView carried for free, now an ordinary
                     label: BindableLayout has no EmptyView, and dropping this line would have left a
                     shift with no closed orders showing a bare heading and nothing under it. It
                     gets its own row so it costs nothing while the list has content — and while
                     it does, the collapsed row costs only the 10dp RowSpacing, which on a page
                     that scrolls is not a measurement that matters. -->
                <!-- Left-aligned for the same reason as «Движений по кассе не было.» above, and by
                     the same local override: EmptyLabel centres every empty state in the app, this
                     page aligns its text to the left everywhere else, and the shared style is not
                     this page's to change. -->
                <Label Grid.Row="8" Text="Закрытых заказов пока нет." Style="{StaticResource EmptyLabel}"
                       HorizontalTextAlignment="Start"
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasNoShiftHistory}" />
                <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                     «СКИДКИ» — THE PRICE CONTROL, AND THE WHOLE OF IT.

                     This section is the feature plan 4.2 asks for, at Tier 1: DETECTION, not
                     prevention. Nothing on this page prevents anything, nothing was refused at the
                     till, and there is deliberately no reason code and no manager PIN here or
                     anywhere else — a justification collected at the till becomes the first option
                     clicked and controls nothing, and this project has no operator entity to hold an
                     approval yet. What it does is make the override VISIBLE to whoever reads the
                     shift afterwards, at zero friction during the sale itself.

                     IT IS NOT PART OF ANY TOTAL ABOVE, and the note under the heading says so on
                     screen rather than leaving it to be inferred from the layout. Two orders' worth
                     of this cannot be added together even in principle: a cancelled order's money
                     went back, so its line is here and its discount is not money anyone kept.
                     Summing it would report a figure that describes nothing.

                     VOIDED ROWS ARE INCLUDED ON PURPOSE and carry a «отменён» pill. A voided sale is
                     precisely where an overridden price is worth seeing — the price was touched and
                     then the sale was undone, which is a mistake twice over — and the domain filters
                     on the price mismatch rather than on the order status for the same reason.

                     WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, so it is not rediscovered as a bug: bundles that
                     are cheaper than their parts ON PURPOSE. The filter is a price mismatch, so a
                     legitimately discounted bundle does not appear. That is documented on
                     IOrderService.GetDiscountedLinesAsync and it is a decision, not an omission.

                     The rows are cards, like the two lists above, and every figure is LABELLED —
                     «Разрешено», «Взимается», «Скидка» — rather than left to three numbers in a row
                     to be told apart. An audit list whose columns have to be guessed at is not an
                     audit list, and on a 360dp card a four-column grid would have had to clip.
                     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="9" Spacing="4" IsVisible="{Binding HasOpenShift}">
                    <Label Text="Скидки" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
                    <Label Text="{Binding DiscountsNote}" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                           LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
                    <!-- Left-aligned for the same reason as the two empty states above, and by the
                         same local override: EmptyLabel centres every empty state in the app and this
                         page aligns its text to the left everywhere else.
                         The whole section is bound to HasOpenShift, like the movements list above:
                         with no shift there is nothing to detect, and an empty «Скидок не было» on a
                         screen that says «Смена не открыта» would claim a shift had none. -->
                    <Label Text="Скидок и пересмотров цены не было." Style="{StaticResource EmptyLabel}"
                           HorizontalTextAlignment="Start"
                           IsVisible="{Binding HasNoDiscountedLines}" />

                    <VerticalStackLayout BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding DiscountedLines}" Spacing="0">
                        <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:DiscountedLineRow">
                                <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="4">
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                            <Label Text="{Binding OrderTitle}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                            <!-- The voided marker. A plain Tag, NOT TagWarning: a void is
                                                 a FACT about the ledger, and an orange pill would claim it
                                                 is a warning. The word carries the state; the pill only
                                                 marks it. Same right edge as the amounts below, so a pill
                                                 appearing cannot shift them out from under the eye. -->
                                            <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource Tag}"
                                                    VerticalOptions="Center" IsVisible="{Binding IsVoided}"
                                                    SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding VoidedHint}">
                                                <Label Text="{Binding VoidedText}" Style="{StaticResource TagText}" />
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>

                                        <Label Text="{Binding LineTitle}" LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
                                        <!-- Variant and modifier ride along on their own line, hidden when
                                             there is neither. A label that printed «Без модификатора» on
                                             every row would be telling the operator something the row
                                             does not know. -->
                                        <Label Text="{Binding ModifierText}" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                               LineBreakMode="WordWrap"
                                               IsVisible="{Binding HasModifierText}" />

                                        <!-- Labelled figures, one per line: quantity, the allowed
                                             price, the price actually charged, and the difference.
                                             Auto,* so the labels keep their width and the amounts align
                                             down the section — which is what makes a column of them
                                             addable by eye, the same reason CashMovementRow signs its
                                             amounts. -->
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8" RowSpacing="1">
                                            <Label Text="Количество" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                                            <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding QuantityText}" />
                                            <Label Grid.Row="1" Text="Разрешено" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                                            <Label Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding AllowedPriceText}" />
                                            <Label Grid.Row="2" Text="Взимается" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                                            <Label Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding ChargedPriceText}" />
                                            <!-- The label is bound, not literal: a price can be RAISED as
                                                 well as lowered, and a section that can only say «Скидка»
                                                 would misname the half of the changes that raise. -->
                                            <Label Grid.Row="3" Text="{Binding DifferenceLabel}" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                                            <Label Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding DifferenceText}"
                                                   FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                        </Grid>

                                        <!-- THE SECOND, INDEPENDENT SIGNAL. Only on a bundle line, and
                                             labelled as what it is: what the same dishes cost on their own.
                                             It is NOT the same figure as the difference above — a bundle
                                             priced at exactly the sum of its slots has nothing to report
                                             here and everything to report there. -->
                                        <Label Text="{Binding BundleText}" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                               LineBreakMode="WordWrap" IsVisible="{Binding HasBundleText}" />
                                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                                </Border>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- No reconciliation block on THIS page, and that is a decision rather than an
                     omission: the page rebinds to whichever shift is open and its route
                     carries no shift id, so it can only ever display the open shift — which by
                     definition has no count. A block here would have been permanently invisible, and
                     the analytics page is the one screen that can read a closed shift.
                     The description carries the one thing the operator must know before pressing it:
                     the count is asked for and the shift does not close without one. -->
                <Button Grid.Row="10" Text="Закрыть смену" Style="{StaticResource DangerButton}"
                        Command="{Binding CloseShiftCommand}"
                        SemanticProperties.Description="Закрыть смену и пересчитать кассу. Будет запрошена сумма, и без неё смена не закроется." />
        </Grid>
    </ScrollView>
</ContentPage>
